# uv upstream pin.
#
# uv is distributed as **precompiled static binaries** — our build scripts
# download the right per-platform archive from GitHub Releases rather than
# building from source. That's why this VERSION file is different from
# the llama-cpp / sd-cpp pattern: no upstream clone, no commit-sha-driven
# checkout, just a tag + per-archive sha256 digests copied from Astral's
# companion `.sha256` files alongside each release asset.
#
# The `commit=` field is the sha the tag points at — used by the shared
# preflight in .github/workflows/build-native.yml to decide whether the
# engine is pinned (non-zero sha) or skippable (all zeros).
#
# How to bump:
#   1. `gh api repos/astral-sh/uv/releases/latest --jq .tag_name`
#   2. `gh api repos/astral-sh/uv/git/refs/tags/<tag> --jq .object.sha`
#   3. For each platform archive, curl the companion `.sha256` from
#      `https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/<tag>/<asset>.sha256`
#      and copy the hex digest below.
#   4. Run `./build.sh` locally to validate, then tag `native-vX.Y.Z`.
#
